# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample-based Krylov Quantum Diagonalization ([SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702)) is a quantum-centric variant of subspace diagonalization. Rather than sampling a single variational ansatz (as in plain sample-based quantum diagonalization ([SQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068))) or an ensemble of randomized time-evolution circuits (as in [SqDRIFT](sqdrift#sqdrift-getting-started)), it samples a *Krylov* basis: the family of states\n"
msgstr "Pepenyetuaan Kuantum Krylov Berasaskan Sampel ([SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702)) ialah varian pepenyetuaan subruang yang berpusatkan kuantum. Daripada mensampel satu ansatz variasi tunggal (seperti dalam pepenyetuaan kuantum berasaskan sampel biasa ([SQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068))) atau satu ensembel litar evolusi masa rawak (seperti dalam [SqDRIFT](sqdrift#sqdrift-getting-started)), ia mensampel asas *Krylov*: keluarga keadaan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_k \\rangle = e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H} \\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle, \\qquad k = 0, 1, \\dots,\n"
"D - 1,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_k \\rangle = e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H} \\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle, \\qquad k = 0, 1, \\dots,\n"
"D - 1,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "obtained by evolving a reference state $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ for increasing multiples of a fixed time step $\\Delta t$. Bitstrings sampled from these $D$ circuits populate the Krylov subspace in which the Hamiltonian is subsequently diagonalized classically.\n"
msgstr "yang diperoleh dengan mengevolusikan keadaan rujukan $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ untuk gandaan yang meningkat bagi langkah masa tetap $\\Delta t$. Rentetan bit yang disampel daripada $D$ litar ini mengisi subruang Krylov yang di dalamnya Hamiltonian kemudiannya dipepenyetuakan secara klasik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide reproduces the circuit-construction step of the [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) algorithm for the single-impurity Anderson model (SIAM), a magnetic impurity coupled to a non-interacting bath, following the [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) publication.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menghasilkan semula langkah pembinaan litar bagi algoritma [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) untuk model Anderson satu-bendasing (SIAM), iaitu bendasing magnetik yang ditambat kepada rendaman tanpa interaksi, mengikut penerbitan [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The SKQD sampling step works only if the ground state is **sparse** in the computational basis: the classical diagonalization must be able to reconstruct it from a manageable number of sampled bitstrings. As shown below, that sparsity is not automatic; it is a property of the single-particle basis in which the problem is expressed. Getting the basis right is the crux of this construction.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Langkah pensampelan SKQD hanya berfungsi jika keadaan asas adalah **jarang** dalam asas pengiraan: pepenyetuaan klasik mesti dapat membinanya semula daripada bilangan rentetan bit sampel yang boleh diurus. Seperti yang ditunjukkan di bawah, kejarangan itu tidak berlaku secara automatik; ia merupakan sifat asas satu-zarah yang digunakan untuk menyatakan masalah. Mendapatkan asas yang betul adalah inti pembinaan ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"build-the-siam-hamiltonian-as-a-fermionic-operator\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Build the SIAM Hamiltonian as a fermionic operator {#1-build-the-siam-hamiltonian-as-a-fermionic-operator}"
msgstr "1. Bina Hamiltonian SIAM sebagai operator fermionik {#1-build-the-siam-hamiltonian-as-a-fermionic-operator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The single-impurity Anderson model places one interacting impurity orbital (index $0$) in contact with a non-interacting bath of $L$ sites arranged as a chain. Its Hamiltonian splits into a one-body part $H_1$ and a two-body part $H_2$,\n"
msgstr "Model Anderson satu-bendasing meletakkan satu orbital bendasing berinteraksi (indeks $0$) bersentuhan dengan rendaman tanpa interaksi berjumlah $L$ tapak yang tersusun sebagai rantai. Hamiltoniannya terbahagi kepada bahagian satu-jasad $H_1$ dan bahagian dua-jasad $H_2$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = H_1 + H_2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = H_1 + H_2,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with the one-body part collecting the impurity on-site energy (the chemical potential $\\mu$), the impurity–bath hybridization $V$, and the nearest-neighbor bath hopping $t$,\n"
msgstr "dengan bahagian satu-jasad mengumpulkan tenaga atas-tapak bendasing (keupayaan kimia $\\mu$), hibridisasi bendasing–rendaman $V$, dan lompatan rendaman jiran terdekat $t$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H_1 = \\mu \\sum_\\sigma a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{0\\sigma}\n"
"      - V \\sum_\\sigma \\left( a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{1\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right)\n"
"      - t \\sum_{\\sigma} \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1}\n"
"        \\left( a^\\dagger_{i\\sigma} a_{i+1,\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H_1 = \\mu \\sum_\\sigma a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{0\\sigma}\n"
"      - V \\sum_\\sigma \\left( a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{1\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right)\n"
"      - t \\sum_{\\sigma} \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1}\n"
"        \\left( a^\\dagger_{i\\sigma} a_{i+1,\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and the two-body part carrying the on-site Coulomb repulsion $U$ on the impurity alone,\n"
msgstr "dan bahagian dua-jasad membawa tolakan Coulomb atas-tapak $U$ pada bendasing sahaja,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H_2 = U \\, a^\\dagger_{0\\uparrow} a_{0\\uparrow} a^\\dagger_{0\\downarrow} a_{0\\downarrow}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H_2 = U \\, a^\\dagger_{0\\uparrow} a_{0\\uparrow} a^\\dagger_{0\\downarrow} a_{0\\downarrow}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide works at the particle-hole-symmetric point $\\mu = -U/2$. These two parts map directly onto the one-body integrals `h1e` (bath hopping, impurity hybridization, impurity on-site energy) and the single two-body integral `h2e` (the impurity Coulomb term). First assemble them in the position basis, where the model is naturally defined.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini bekerja pada titik simetri zarah-lohong $\\mu = -U/2$. Kedua-dua bahagian ini dipetakan terus kepada kamiran satu-jasad `h1e` (lompatan rendaman, hibridisasi bendasing, tenaga atas-tapak bendasing) dan kamiran dua-jasad tunggal `h2e` (sebutan Coulomb bendasing). Mula-mula himpunkannya dalam asas kedudukan, iaitu tempat model ditakrifkan secara semula jadi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"change-to-the-momentum-basis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Change to the momentum basis {#2-change-to-the-momentum-basis}"
msgstr "2. Tukar kepada asas momentum {#2-change-to-the-momentum-basis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bath part of the SIAM is a free-fermion chain, so it is diagonalized by a change to the momentum basis. This is the decisive step for SKQD. Because the bath is translationally invariant, the ground state is not sparse in the position basis, but it is sparse in the momentum basis, where the bath Hamiltonian is diagonal. The single-particle orbital rotation that performs this change is problem-specific linear algebra. It diagonalizes the bath hopping matrix while leaving the impurity orbital untouched, then relocates the impurity to a central site:\n"
msgstr "Bahagian rendaman SIAM ialah rantai fermion bebas, jadi ia dipepenyetuakan oleh pertukaran kepada asas momentum. Ini ialah langkah penentu bagi SKQD. Oleh kerana rendaman tidak berubah terhadap translasi, keadaan asas tidak jarang dalam asas kedudukan, tetapi jarang dalam asas momentum, yang di dalamnya Hamiltonian rendaman adalah pepenjuru. Putaran orbital satu-zarah yang melakukan pertukaran ini ialah algebra linear khusus masalah. Ia memepenjurukan matriks lompatan rendaman sambil membiarkan orbital bendasing tidak disentuh, kemudian memindahkan bendasing ke tapak tengah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlike a variational workflow, this rotates the Hamiltonian integrals into the momentum basis, so that the whole circuit (Hamiltonian and state alike) lives in the basis where the ground state is sparse and the sampled bitstrings are therefore informative. Rotating the one- and two-body integrals is a standard basis change of the electronic-structure tensors:\n"
msgstr "Tidak seperti aliran kerja variasi, ini memutarkan kamiran Hamiltonian ke dalam asas momentum, supaya keseluruhan litar (Hamiltonian dan keadaan sekali gus) berada dalam asas yang keadaan asasnya jarang dan rentetan bit yang disampel oleh itu bermaklumat. Memutarkan kamiran satu- dan dua-jasad ialah perubahan asas piawai bagi tensor struktur elektronik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the rotation leaves the impurity orbital fixed (it acts only on the bath), the on-site interaction is unchanged. `h2e_momentum` remains a single number-number term, just like `h2e`. The only change is that the impurity has been relocated to a central index. This is visible directly in the integral tensors, which each carry one nonzero entry:\n"
msgstr "Oleh kerana putaran membiarkan orbital bendasing tetap (ia hanya bertindak pada rendaman), interaksi atas-tapak tidak berubah. `h2e_momentum` kekal sebagai satu sebutan nombor-nombor tunggal, sama seperti `h2e`. Satu-satunya perubahan ialah bendasing telah dipindahkan ke indeks tengah. Ini kelihatan terus dalam tensor kamiran, yang masing-masing membawa satu entri bukan sifar:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This locality is what keeps the interaction cheap to synthesize later.\n"
msgstr "Kelokalan inilah yang menjadikan interaksi murah untuk disintesis kemudian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assemble the one-body integrals into a [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") with the electronic-integral constructor [`from_1body_tril_spin_sym()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym\"), which expects them packed into lower-triangular ordering. The two-body part is a single number-number term, so rather than routing it through the two-body integral machinery, build it directly with [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-cre#qiskit_fermions.operators.cre \"qiskit_fermions.operators.cre\")/[`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-ann#qiskit_fermions.operators.ann \"qiskit_fermions.operators.ann\"): the on-site Coulomb operator $U \\, n_{p\\uparrow} n_{p\\downarrow}$ for the impurity mode $p$ (its $\\uparrow$ mode at index `p`, its $\\downarrow$ mode at index `p + norb` in the block-spin layout). Both constructors spin-double the `norb` spatial orbitals into `2 * norb` fermionic modes.\n"
msgstr "Himpunkan kamiran satu-jasad ke dalam [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") dengan pembina kamiran elektronik [`from_1body_tril_spin_sym()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym\"), yang menjangkakan ia dipek dalam susunan segi tiga bawah. Bahagian dua-jasad ialah satu sebutan nombor-nombor tunggal, jadi daripada menyalurkannya melalui jentera kamiran dua-jasad, bina terus dengan [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-cre#qiskit_fermions.operators.cre \"qiskit_fermions.operators.cre\")/[`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-ann#qiskit_fermions.operators.ann \"qiskit_fermions.operators.ann\"): operator Coulomb atas-tapak $U \\, n_{p\\uparrow} n_{p\\downarrow}$ untuk mod bendasing $p$ (mod $\\uparrow$ pada indeks `p`, mod $\\downarrow$ pada indeks `p + norb` dalam susun atur spin berblok). Kedua-dua pembina menggandakan spin bagi `norb` orbital ruang kepada `2 * norb` mod fermionik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the one-body part $H_1$ and the two-body part $H_2$ as separate operators rather than summing them eagerly, matching the terms $H_1$ and $H_2$ of the section-1 equations. Building each piece once (in both bases) makes them reusable below. Summed, they give the full Hamiltonian for the exact diagonalization in either basis. Individually, $H_2$ (momentum basis) is the operator the Trotter step evolves in step 4.\n"
msgstr "Kekalkan bahagian satu-jasad $H_1$ dan bahagian dua-jasad $H_2$ sebagai operator berasingan dan bukannya menjumlahkannya serta-merta, sepadan dengan sebutan $H_1$ dan $H_2$ dalam persamaan bahagian 1. Membina setiap bahagian sekali (dalam kedua-dua asas) menjadikannya boleh digunakan semula di bawah. Apabila dijumlahkan, ia memberikan Hamiltonian penuh untuk pepenyetuaan tepat dalam mana-mana asas. Secara individu, $H_2$ (asas momentum) ialah operator yang dievolusikan oleh langkah Trotter dalam langkah 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The basis change is a unitary similarity transform, so it leaves the spectrum untouched. Confirm the operator is correct by comparing its lowest eigenvalue in the $(\\text{norb}, \\text{nelec})$ sector against an exact diagonalization. The [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") exposes a SciPy [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") (backed by a native full configuration interaction (FCI) matrix-vector kernel), so it can be handed straight to [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\").\n"
msgstr "Perubahan asas ialah transformasi keserupaan uniter, jadi ia tidak mengubah spektrum. Sahkan operator itu betul dengan membandingkan nilai eigen terendahnya dalam sektor $(\\text{norb}, \\text{nelec})$ dengan pepenyetuaan tepat. [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") mendedahkan [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") SciPy (disokong oleh kernel hasil darab matriks-vektor interaksi konfigurasi penuh (FCI) asli), jadi ia boleh diserahkan terus kepada [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payoff of the basis change is sparsity. To make it concrete, count how many computational-basis determinants are needed to capture 99% of the ground-state weight, and compare the momentum basis against the position basis. The energy is basis-independent, but the number of determinants is not:\n"
msgstr "Kelebihan perubahan asas ialah kejarangan. Untuk menjadikannya konkrit, kira berapa banyak penentu asas pengiraan diperlukan untuk menangkap 99% berat keadaan asas, dan bandingkan asas momentum dengan asas kedudukan. Tenaga adalah bebas asas, tetapi bilangan penentu tidak:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two operators share the same energy, but the position-basis ground state is spread over thousands of determinants, while the momentum basis concentrates it onto around 20, which is why SKQD sampling works in the momentum basis and not the position basis.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua operator berkongsi tenaga yang sama, tetapi keadaan asas dalam asas kedudukan tersebar merentasi beribu-ribu penentu, manakala asas momentum menumpukannya kepada sekitar 20, itulah sebabnya pensampelan SKQD berfungsi dalam asas momentum dan bukan asas kedudukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"prepare-the-reference-state\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Prepare the reference state {#3-prepare-the-reference-state}"
msgstr "3. Sediakan keadaan rujukan {#3-prepare-the-reference-state}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The SKQD reference $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ is the superposition of all excitations of the electrons closest to the Fermi level into the nearest empty momentum modes. The [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) publication builds it with a hand-written network of [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)s. It looks strongly correlated (it has hundreds of nonzero computational-basis amplitudes), but a network of number-conserving two-mode rotations is a single-particle (fermionic Gaussian) operation, so the state it produces is a single Slater determinant. That means you can prepare it with one [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate, given the single-particle rotation the network implements.\n"
msgstr "Rujukan SKQD $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ ialah superposisi semua pengujaan elektron yang paling hampir dengan aras Fermi ke dalam mod momentum kosong terdekat. Penerbitan [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) membinanya dengan rangkaian [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) yang ditulis tangan. Ia kelihatan berkorelasi kuat (ia mempunyai ratusan amplitud asas pengiraan bukan sifar), tetapi rangkaian putaran dua-mod yang memelihara nombor ialah operasi satu-zarah (Gauss fermionik), jadi keadaan yang dihasilkannya ialah satu penentu Slater tunggal. Itu bermakna anda boleh menyediakannya dengan satu Gate [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"), dengan putaran satu-zarah yang dilaksanakan oleh rangkaian itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because each [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) acts as a Givens rotation on a pair of modes, that rotation can be built directly in the single-particle picture (one Givens matrix per gate) instead of emitting the two-qubit gates by hand. The gates form a brickwork of nearest-neighbor rotations that fans out from the Fermi level in expanding layers, spreading each near-Fermi electron across the empty modes just above it:\n"
msgstr "Oleh kerana setiap [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) bertindak sebagai putaran Givens pada sepasang mod, putaran itu boleh dibina terus dalam gambaran satu-zarah (satu matriks Givens bagi setiap Gate) dan bukannya mengeluarkan Gate dua-qubit secara manual. Gate ini membentuk kerja bata putaran jiran terdekat yang mengembang dari aras Fermi dalam lapisan yang meluas, menyebarkan setiap elektron berhampiran Fermi merentasi mod kosong tepat di atasnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The rotation above is expressed in the momentum basis, matching the Hamiltonian. The electrons near the Fermi level are the highest-energy occupied momentum modes, and the network excites them into the lowest-energy empty ones. This is why the reference must be built after the basis change of the previous step, not before.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Putaran di atas dinyatakan dalam asas momentum, sepadan dengan Hamiltonian. Elektron berhampiran aras Fermi ialah mod momentum diduduki bertenaga tertinggi, dan rangkaian itu mengujakannya ke dalam mod kosong bertenaga terendah. Inilah sebabnya rujukan mesti dibina selepas perubahan asas pada langkah sebelumnya, bukan sebelumnya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Slater determinant preparation is done per spin sector, since each sector has its own (electrons, orbitals) shape. A single [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate (an occupation, the lowest `nocc` modes filled, together with the single-particle rotation) prepares one sector; the same gate is applied once on the alpha modes `0..norb` and once on the beta modes `norb..2*norb`, since both spin sectors share the same reference occupation and rotation here:\n"
msgstr "Penyediaan penentu Slater dilakukan bagi setiap sektor spin, kerana setiap sektor mempunyai bentuk (elektron, orbital) tersendiri. Satu Gate [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") (satu penghunian, mod `nocc` terendah diisi, bersama putaran satu-zarah) menyediakan satu sektor; Gate yang sama dikenakan sekali pada mod alfa `0..norb` dan sekali pada mod beta `norb..2*norb`, kerana kedua-dua sektor spin berkongsi penghunian dan putaran rujukan yang sama di sini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This declarative gate replaces the hand-coded [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) network; the transpiler generates the Givens-rotation synthesis.\n"
msgstr "Gate deklaratif ini menggantikan rangkaian [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) yang dikod tangan; Transpiler menjana sintesis putaran Givens.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"assemble-the-krylov-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Assemble the Krylov circuits {#4-assemble-the-krylov-circuits}"
msgstr "4. Himpunkan litar Krylov {#4-assemble-the-krylov-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each Krylov circuit is the reference-state preparation followed by evolution under $e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H}$. Split the Hamiltonian into its one-body and two-body parts, $H = H_1 + H_2$, and Trotterize the evolution over that split. This is the decisive choice for circuit depth. The one-body evolution $e^{-i t H_1}$ is a free-fermion (fermionic Gaussian) operation, so it is a single-particle basis rotation (an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") with unitary $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$) rather than something that has to be Pauli-Trotterized term by term. The two-body evolution $e^{-i t H_2}$ acts only on the single on-site interaction term. Building the step this way lets the transpiler emit a shallow brickwork of Givens rotations plus a single two-qubit interaction gate, the shallow structure that the [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) publication builds by hand.\n"
msgstr "Setiap litar Krylov ialah penyediaan keadaan rujukan diikuti evolusi di bawah $e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H}$. Pisahkan Hamiltonian kepada bahagian satu-jasad dan dua-jasadnya, $H = H_1 + H_2$, dan lakukan Trotterisasi evolusi ke atas pembahagian itu. Ini ialah pilihan penentu bagi kedalaman litar. Evolusi satu-jasad $e^{-i t H_1}$ ialah operasi fermion bebas (Gauss fermionik), jadi ia ialah putaran asas satu-zarah (satu [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") dengan uniter $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$) dan bukannya sesuatu yang perlu ditrotterkan secara Pauli sebutan demi sebutan. Evolusi dua-jasad $e^{-i t H_2}$ hanya bertindak pada sebutan interaksi atas-tapak tunggal. Membina langkah dengan cara ini membolehkan Transpiler menghasilkan kerja bata putaran Givens yang cetek ditambah satu Gate interaksi dua-qubit, struktur cetek yang dibina secara manual oleh penerbitan [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We already have the two-body part. It is the `two_body_momentum` operator built in step 2 (the single on-site term). The one-body evolution $e^{-i t H_1}$ is spin-independent, so it is a single per-sector [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") with unitary $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$ applied once to each spin sector, the same parallel structure as the reference-state preparation.\n"
msgstr "Kita sudah mempunyai bahagian dua-jasad. Ia ialah operator `two_body_momentum` yang dibina pada langkah 2 (sebutan atas-tapak tunggal). Evolusi satu-jasad $e^{-i t H_1}$ adalah bebas spin, jadi ia ialah satu [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") bagi setiap sektor dengan uniter $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$ yang dikenakan sekali pada setiap sektor spin, struktur selari yang sama seperti penyediaan keadaan rujukan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each Krylov circuit evolves for a total time $k \\, \\Delta t$. That is realized with a second-order Trotter product of $k$ steps of size $\\Delta t$, so the per-step error stays fixed as the Krylov dimension grows. Each step sandwiches a full one-body rotation (one per spin sector) between two half-steps of the (cheap, single-term) two-body evolution. The Krylov dimension $D$ is the number of such circuits, with `dim` ranging from `0` (reference state only) to $D - 1$.\n"
msgstr "Setiap litar Krylov berevolusi untuk jumlah masa $k \\, \\Delta t$. Ini direalisasikan dengan hasil darab Trotter tertib kedua bagi $k$ langkah bersaiz $\\Delta t$, supaya ralat bagi setiap langkah kekal tetap apabila dimensi Krylov membesar. Setiap langkah mengapit satu putaran satu-jasad penuh (satu bagi setiap sektor spin) di antara dua separuh langkah evolusi dua-jasad (murah, sebutan tunggal). Dimensi Krylov $D$ ialah bilangan litar sedemikian, dengan `dim` berjulat dari `0` (keadaan rujukan sahaja) hingga $D - 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The circuits built here carry no measurements yet, because the same fermionic circuits also drive the exact simulation in step 6, and a measurement is not a unitary operation. Step 5 adds them with [`FermionicCircuit.measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\"), which reads mode `i` into classical bit `i`.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Litar yang dibina di sini belum membawa pengukuran, kerana litar fermionik yang sama juga memacu simulasi tepat pada langkah 6, dan pengukuran bukan operasi uniter. Langkah 5 menambahkannya dengan [`FermionicCircuit.measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\"), yang membaca mod `i` ke dalam bit klasik `i`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Prefer measuring the *fermionic* circuit over the transpiled one. A fermionic measurement names the mode it reads, so layout and routing carry it along with the qubit that mode ended up on, and the sampled bitstring is indexed by mode. Measuring the transpiled circuit instead leaves you to undo [`final_index_layout()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.TranspileLayout#final_index_layout) yourself, and silently returns permuted results if you forget. This relies on the occupation-basis Jordan-Wigner encoding the preset uses, where each mode is carried by one qubit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Utamakan mengukur litar *fermionik* berbanding litar yang telah ditranspilasi. Pengukuran fermionik menamakan mod yang dibacanya, jadi susun atur dan penghalaan membawanya bersama qubit yang menjadi tempat mod itu berakhir, dan rentetan bit yang disampel diindeks mengikut mod. Mengukur litar yang telah ditranspilasi sebaliknya meninggalkan anda untuk membatalkan [`final_index_layout()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.TranspileLayout#final_index_layout) sendiri, dan secara senyap mengembalikan keputusan yang ditukar tertib jika anda terlupa. Ini bergantung pada pengekodan Jordan-Wigner asas penghunian yang digunakan oleh pratetap, yang setiap mod dibawa oleh satu qubit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpile-to-qubit-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Transpile to qubit circuits {#5-transpile-to-qubit-circuits}"
msgstr "5. Transpilasi kepada litar qubit {#5-transpile-to-qubit-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpiling a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") maps its fermionic gates to qubit gates. This uses the Jordan-Wigner [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") mapping. The [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates synthesize into a brickwork of Givens rotations, and the single-term [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") lowers to a single two-qubit interaction gate.\n"
msgstr "Transpilasi [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") memetakan Gate fermioniknya kepada Gate qubit. Ini menggunakan pemetaan Jordan-Wigner [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\"). Gate [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") disintesis kepada kerja bata putaran Givens, dan [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") sebutan tunggal diturunkan kepada satu Gate interaksi dua-qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because every fermionic gate here has a default synthesis, you can use the ready-made [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") directly rather than hand-assembling the stages. Any keyword arguments are forwarded to the qubit stage; pass `optimization_level=0` for a faithful, unoptimized picture of the synthesized depth. Generating the full family of Krylov circuits is then a loop over the Krylov dimension. Keep the untranspiled [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")s alongside the transpiled qubit circuits. The fermionic ones drive the exact (statevector) simulation in step 6, so they must stay measurement-free; `measure_all(inplace=False)` returns a measured copy to transpile and leaves the original untouched, and that copy is what a backend would execute.\n"
msgstr "Oleh kerana setiap Gate fermionik di sini mempunyai sintesis lalai, anda boleh menggunakan [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") yang siap sedia terus dan bukannya menghimpun peringkat secara manual. Sebarang argumen kata kunci dimajukan kepada peringkat qubit; hantar `optimization_level=0` untuk gambaran setia dan tidak dioptimumkan bagi kedalaman yang disintesis. Menjana keseluruhan keluarga litar Krylov kemudiannya ialah gelung ke atas dimensi Krylov. Simpan [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") yang belum ditranspilasi bersama litar qubit yang telah ditranspilasi. Yang fermionik memacu simulasi tepat (vektor keadaan) pada langkah 6, jadi ia mesti kekal bebas pengukuran; `measure_all(inplace=False)` mengembalikan salinan yang diukur untuk ditranspilasi dan membiarkan yang asal tidak disentuh, dan salinan itulah yang akan dilaksanakan oleh Backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Krylov dimension shows up directly in the circuits’ two-qubit depth. The reference-state preparation is a fixed cost, and each additional Krylov power adds another second-order Trotter step of the time-evolution operator.\n"
msgstr "Dimensi Krylov kelihatan terus dalam kedalaman dua-qubit litar. Penyediaan keadaan rujukan ialah kos tetap, dan setiap kuasa Krylov tambahan menambah satu lagi langkah Trotter tertib kedua bagi operator evolusi masa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Splitting the Hamiltonian keeps these depths modest. The one-body evolution is a genuine orbital rotation, so it synthesizes to an [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) brickwork on adjacent qubits. Each half step of the on-site interaction is a single [`RZZGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RZZGate) coupling the impurity’s two spin modes; the cheap term that the second-order product sandwiches around the rotation. Handing the whole Hamiltonian to one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate instead would Pauli-Trotterize the one-body part term by term, propagating long Jordan-Wigner `Z`-strings across the (long-range) impurity-bath couplings and inflating the depth by an order of magnitude.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Memisahkan Hamiltonian memastikan kedalaman ini sederhana. Evolusi satu-jasad ialah putaran orbital sebenar, jadi ia disintesis kepada kerja bata [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) pada qubit bersebelahan. Setiap separuh langkah interaksi atas-tapak ialah satu [`RZZGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RZZGate) yang menggandingkan dua mod spin bendasing; sebutan murah yang diapit oleh hasil darab tertib kedua di sekeliling putaran. Menyerahkan keseluruhan Hamiltonian kepada satu Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") sebaliknya akan mentrotterkan secara Pauli bahagian satu-jasad sebutan demi sebutan, merambatkan rentetan `Z` Jordan-Wigner yang panjang merentasi gandingan bendasing-rendaman (jarak jauh) dan membengkakkan kedalaman sebanyak satu tertib magnitud.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first circuit prepares only the reference determinant, while the last carries the most Trotter steps (four in this case):\n"
msgstr "Litar pertama hanya menyediakan penentu rujukan, manakala yang terakhir membawa langkah Trotter paling banyak (empat dalam kes ini):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The reference-state preparation circuit (Krylov dimension 0).](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-13.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The reference-state preparation circuit (Krylov dimension 0).](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-13.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A second-order Trotter Krylov circuit with four evolution steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-14.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A second-order Trotter Krylov circuit with four evolution steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-14.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Sample bitstrings from the Krylov circuits {#6-sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits}"
msgstr "6. Sampelkan rentetan bit daripada litar Krylov {#6-sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On hardware, you would run the transpiled circuits and measure. This is the noiseless (statevector) version of that step, showing the bitstrings SKQD would collect. Simulate each untranspiled [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") with [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") and sample the resulting statevector with [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\").\n"
msgstr "Pada perkakasan, anda akan menjalankan litar yang telah ditranspilasi dan mengukur. Ini ialah versi tanpa hingar (vektor keadaan) bagi langkah itu, yang menunjukkan rentetan bit yang akan dikumpulkan oleh SKQD. Simulasikan setiap [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") yang belum ditranspilasi dengan [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") dan sampelkan vektor keadaan yang terhasil dengan [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate is validate-then-rotate under simulation (it checks that the incoming state occupies its reference determinant, then applies the rotation). Therefore, the input is the plain occupation determinant: the lowest `nocc` modes filled per spin, with no rotation. The gate applies `reference_rotation` itself.\n"
msgstr "Gate [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") ialah sahkan-kemudian-putar di bawah simulasi (ia menyemak bahawa keadaan masukan menduduki penentu rujukannya, kemudian mengenakan putaran). Oleh itu, masukan ialah penentu penghunian biasa: mod `nocc` terendah diisi bagi setiap spin, tanpa putaran. Gate itu mengenakan `reference_rotation` sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pooling the samples from all five Krylov circuits, the support is tiny: a few hundred distinct bitstrings out of the $\\binom{8}{4}^2 = 4900$ determinants in the `(4, 4)` sector. This concentration, a direct consequence of the momentum-basis sparsity established in step 2, makes the subsequent classical diagonalization tractable.\n"
msgstr "Dengan menggabungkan sampel daripada kesemua lima litar Krylov, sokongannya sangat kecil: beberapa ratus rentetan bit berbeza daripada $\\binom{8}{4}^2 = 4900$ penentu dalam sektor `(4, 4)`. Penumpuan ini, akibat langsung kejarangan asas momentum yang ditetapkan pada langkah 2, menjadikan pepenyetuaan klasik seterusnya boleh dilaksanakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plotting the counts with [`qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram) makes the sparsity visible. A few configurations dominate, led by the reference determinant.\n"
msgstr "Memplot kiraan dengan [`qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram) menjadikan sifat jarang (sparsity) kelihatan. Beberapa konfigurasi mendominasi, diketuai oleh penentu rujukan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Histogram of the bitstrings sampled from the Krylov circuits, showing a small support.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-16.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Histogram of the bitstrings sampled from the Krylov circuits, showing a small support.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-16.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"diagonalize-in-the-sampled-subspace\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Diagonalize in the sampled subspace {#7-diagonalize-in-the-sampled-subspace}"
msgstr "7. Pepenyetelan pepenjuru dalam subruang yang disampel {#7-diagonalize-in-the-sampled-subspace}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sampled bitstrings are the input to the classical half of SKQD. The Hamiltonian is projected onto the subspace the sampled configurations span and diagonalized there. This is passed to the [qiskit-addon-sqd](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd) package, whose [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"(in Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD))\") runs the full sample-based quantum diagonalization loop. It builds a subspace from batches of the sampled configurations, diagonalizes the Hamiltonian in it, and iteratively refines the subspace by using configuration recovery: flipping occupations to repair configurations that violate the known particle-number symmetry. Configuration recovery is designed to undo the damage of hardware noise, which corrupts sampled bitstrings into the wrong particle-number sector; the sampling here is noiseless, so there is nothing to repair on that front.\n"
msgstr "Rentetan bit yang disampel ialah input kepada separuh klasik SKQD. Hamiltonian diunjurkan ke atas subruang yang dijangkau oleh konfigurasi yang disampel dan dipepenjurukan di sana. Ini diserahkan kepada pakej [qiskit-addon-sqd](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd), yang [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"(in Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD))\") menjalankan keseluruhan gelung pepenjuruan kuantum berasaskan sampel. Ia membina subruang daripada kelompok konfigurasi yang disampel, memepenjurukan Hamiltonian di dalamnya, dan memperhalusi subruang secara berulang dengan menggunakan pemulihan konfigurasi: membalikkan penghunian untuk membaiki konfigurasi yang melanggar simetri bilangan zarah yang diketahui. Pemulihan konfigurasi direka untuk membatalkan kerosakan akibat hingar perkakasan, yang merosakkan rentetan bit yang disampel ke dalam sektor bilangan zarah yang salah; persampelan di sini bebas hingar, jadi tiada apa yang perlu dibaiki dalam hal itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The solver consumes the sampled counts as a [`BitArray`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BitArray), built directly from the pooled `counts` of step 6. Pass `num_bits` explicitly: without it, the width is inferred from the widest sampled bitstring, which is narrower than `2 * norb` whenever no sample occupies the last mode, and the solver then rejects the array. The solver diagonalizes in the same momentum basis the rest of the construction uses, so it takes the `h1e_momentum` and `h2e_momentum` integrals from step 2 directly, with no repacking. The recovered energy matches the exact reference to well under a milli-Hartree, from only a few hundred sampled configurations. Because the SQD energy is a variational upper bound on the true ground state, it always sits at or above `reference_energy` (still in scope from step 2):\n"
msgstr "Penyelesai menggunakan kiraan yang disampel sebagai [`BitArray`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BitArray), yang dibina terus daripada `counts` terkumpul langkah 6. Berikan `num_bits` secara eksplisit: tanpanya, lebar disimpulkan daripada rentetan bit disampel yang paling lebar, yang lebih sempit daripada `2 * norb` apabila tiada sampel menghuni mod terakhir, dan penyelesai kemudian menolak tatasusunan itu. Penyelesai memepenjurukan dalam asas momentum yang sama yang digunakan oleh seluruh pembinaan lain, jadi ia mengambil kamiran `h1e_momentum` dan `h2e_momentum` daripada langkah 2 secara terus, tanpa pembungkusan semula. Tenaga yang dipulihkan sepadan dengan rujukan tepat sehingga jauh di bawah satu mili-Hartree, daripada hanya beberapa ratus konfigurasi yang disampel. Oleh sebab tenaga SQD ialah batas atas variasi bagi keadaan dasar sebenar, ia sentiasa berada pada atau di atas `reference_energy` (masih dalam skop daripada langkah 2):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the run: the energy’s convergence across the iterations, and the average occupancy of each spatial orbital in the recovered ground state. The per-iteration energy is the lowest across that iteration’s batches, and the occupancy sums the `orbital_occupancies` over the two spin sectors. Even without noise to correct, the energy decreases from iteration to iteration. Each iteration diagonalizes within `num_batches` batches of only `samples_per_batch` configurations subsampled from the pool, and the iterative refinement due to bitstring carryover steadily improves which configurations land in those batches, so the recovered energy improves:\n"
msgstr "Visualisasikan larian: penumpuan tenaga merentasi lelaran, dan purata penghunian setiap orbital ruang dalam keadaan dasar yang dipulihkan. Tenaga setiap lelaran ialah yang terendah merentasi kelompok lelaran itu, dan penghunian menjumlahkan `orbital_occupancies` merentasi dua sektor spin. Walaupun tanpa hingar untuk dibetulkan, tenaga berkurang dari lelaran ke lelaran. Setiap lelaran memepenjurukan dalam `num_batches` kelompok yang hanya terdiri daripada `samples_per_batch` konfigurasi yang disubsampel daripada kolam, dan penghalusan berulang akibat pembawaan rentetan bit meningkatkan secara berterusan konfigurasi yang masuk ke dalam kelompok tersebut, sehingga tenaga yang dipulihkan bertambah baik:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![SQD energy convergence and the average occupancy per spatial orbital.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-18.avif)\n"
msgstr "![SQD energy convergence and the average occupancy per spatial orbital.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-18.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This closes the SKQD loop. The momentum-basis circuits of steps 1–5 produce a sparse sample (step 6), and the sample-based diagonalization above turns that sample back into a ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr "Ini melengkapkan gelung SKQD. Litar asas momentum bagi langkah 1–5 menghasilkan sampel jarang (langkah 6), dan pepenjuruan berasaskan sampel di atas menukarkan sampel itu kembali menjadi tenaga keadaan dasar.\n"

